Subject: aacparse: restore the synchronized frame-input minimum

Initial synchronization retains next-frame-size + ADTS_MAX_SIZE as GstBaseParse's
minimum. A smaller complete final ADTS packet then waits for EOS or unrelated
future input. Raw AAC MSE appends need each complete packet before updateend.

After synchronization the seven-byte ADTS header supplies the current packet
size. Retain incomplete packet bytes through needed_data, then reset the minimum
to the header length after a complete frame. Preserve the larger lookahead while
lost-sync validation is required.

MavericksSupport/tests/aac-parser-append covers byte identity, five append sizes,
partial final-frame completion, truncated EOS, resync, and seven/nine-byte headers.

--- a/gst/audioparsers/gstaacparse.c
+++ b/gst/audioparsers/gstaacparse.c
@@ -459,6 +459,16 @@
        to get the correct sync, and this avoids losing two frames when
        a single bit corruption happens. */
     if (drain || !GST_BASE_PARSE_LOST_SYNC (aacparse)) {
+      /* Once synchronized, the current header supplies the frame size.
+       * Do not retain the next-frame lookahead threshold from sync detection:
+       * a shorter complete final frame must not wait for more input or EOS.
+       * The lost-sync branch below restores lookahead when it is needed. */
+      if (*framesize > avail) {
+        *needed_data = *framesize;
+        gst_base_parse_set_min_frame_size (GST_BASE_PARSE (aacparse), *framesize);
+        return FALSE;
+      }
+      gst_base_parse_set_min_frame_size (GST_BASE_PARSE (aacparse), ADTS_HEADERS_LENGTH);
       return TRUE;
     }
 
